To establish property ef{item:independence}, notice that the coin tosses of vertex $u$ determine the decisions of $\mathcal{A}$ to match across $u$. Matching across $u$ decreases $|\mathit{C}_{v}(t)|$ by $2$, hence it does not affect its parity. \par Property ef{item:match-on-top} is proved by recalling that matching on top of $v$ at time $t$ is realized by matching a request located in some leaf $x \in \mathcal{L}(v)$ to a request located in some leaf $x' \in \mathcal{L} - \mathcal{L}(v)$. Since $v 
eq \mathrm{lca}(x, x')$, it must belong to the stilt in $\mathcal{S}(t)$ whose foot is $x$ which establishes the assertion by the definition of $\mathcal{S}(t)$. \par Finally, observe that property ef{item:match-across} holds trivially if $\mathcal{A}$ matched across $v$ at time $t$ because this means that $u_{1}, u_{2} \in \mathit{D}(t)$ and thus, $v, u_{1}, u_{2} 
otin \mathit{D}(t + d t)$. Otherwise, if $\mathcal{A}$ matched on top of $v$ at time $t$, then $v \in \mathit{D}(t)$ which means that $u_{i} \in \mathit{D}(t)$ and $u_{3 - i} 
otin \mathit{D}(t)$ for some $i \in \{ 1, 2 \}$. This also means that $\mathcal{A}$ matched on top of $u_{i}$ at time $t$, therefore $v, u_{i}, u_{3 - i} 
otin \mathit{D}(t + d t)$.

